# CAMEL OVERKILL: LIGHT SHOW. Takes the alert core's light colour (7305) and sends it to every main light (7303),
# unless party mode is on (rainbow). Split out of the alert core: a circuit box holds at most 64 parts.
name camel_lightshow
box battery
note "LIGHT SHOW: HOW IT WORKS" "Normally passes the alert colour (wifi 7305) to the lights (7303).\n'lights party' on the CamelOS bus (7300) switches a multiplexer to a rainbow: an oscillator sawtooth x 360 is the hue of an HSV colour. 'lights claude' paints the whole sub Claude orange. 'lights normal' switches back."
note "WIRING" "No wires: wifi only (7300 and 7305 in, 7303 out)."
c rxa wifi Channel=7305
c rxc wifi Channel=7300
c txk wifi Channel=7303
c pOn regex Expression="^(?i)lights party$" Output=1 FalseOutput="" ContinuousOutput=false
c pOff regex Expression="^(?i)lights normal$" Output=0 FalseOutput="" ContinuousOutput=false
c pCl regex Expression="^(?i)lights claude$" Output=2 FalseOutput="" ContinuousOutput=false
c party mem Value=0
c orange mem Value="217,119,87,255"   # Claude orange
w rxc.out pOn.in pOff.in pCl.in
w pCl.out party.in
w orange.out psel.signal_in2
w pOn.out party.in
w pOff.out party.in
c osc osc OutputType=Sawtooth Frequency=0.2
c k360 mem Value=360
c hue mul
c one mem Value=1
c k255 mem Value=255
c hsv color UseHSV=true
w osc.out hue.1
w k360.out hue.2
w hue.out hsv.signal_r
w one.out hsv.signal_g hsv.signal_b
w k255.out hsv.signal_a
c psel mux
w party.out psel.set_input
w rxa.out psel.signal_in0
w hsv.out psel.signal_in1
w psel.out txk.in
